page('company','About VenueAlign','A shared record of what the tour asks for and what each room can supply.',hero('Company','A shared record before load-in.','VenueAlign is a research-stage concept for the people who advance a tour. Its purpose is to give producers and technical leads evidence they can inspect before a crew arrives.',cta('demo','Inspect Meridian Hall','dark'),'<figure class="subphoto"><img src="assets/model-workshop.webp" alt="Painted touring model and hand-drawn plans in the workshop"></figure>')+section('What we want to learn',steps([('Vision','Give touring teams a shared record of the show requirements and the equipment, space and staff each venue can actually supply.'),('Mission','Link extracted rider lines to their passages, suggest dated venue matches, flag uncertain substitutions and preserve the technical lead’s decision.'),('First commitment','Ask a production manager to fund a Venue Fit evaluation. Review the scorecard together before proposing a broader rollout.')]))+close())
page('validation','Validation plan','Pilot gates, acquisition tests, expansion hypotheses and commercial evidence.',hero('Research notebook','What has to be true?','The commercial model, integration effort, accuracy and buyer commitments remain hypotheses. Use the evaluation to test them against actual advance decisions.',cta('results','Inspect the scorecard','dark'),visual=scenic.supporting_visual('validation'))+section('The buying sequence',steps([('Inspect the case','Start on an offer page and open the fictional Meridian Hall walkthrough. Compare it with a past buyer-owned case.'),('Fund the comparison','Confirm budget and data access. Identify the signer, data owner, technical reviewer per stop and renewal owner. Sign the scope and agree on the baseline.'),('Review the result','Run the matched comparison and review time, valid substitutions, unsupported fits and adverse outcomes with the buyer.')]))+section('Reach the people who own the advance',noteitems([('LinkedIn and partner outreach','Reach touring production managers, production suppliers and venue networks with a short teardown of the fixture exception. Invite the workflow owner to bring a past case.'),('Variant A','Find the rider requirements a venue still needs to resolve.'),('Variant B','Inspect an annotated Venue Fit exception packet, then compare the decision with your own advance.'),('Traffic test','Compare qualified meetings, data permission and paid evaluation interest across both messages. Record spend and consent separately. Use measured claims only after an authorized comparison.')]))+section('Expansion and commercial test',noteitems([('Distribution','Test distribution through rental houses and venue networks. With authorization, approved venue capability profiles could be reused by multiple tours.'),('Recurring demand','At the $18,000 annual hypothesis, 56 equivalent customers would produce $1,008,000 in annual recurring revenue. Validate reachable buyers, implementation cost and renewal before treating that arithmetic as a forecast.'),('Decision gate','Proceed beyond preview only when a budget owner funds the evaluation, the records owner authorizes data and a named reviewer accepts the comparison protocol.')]))+section('Later operations tracking','<p class="lead">The proposed Notion record tracks buyer, named operator, integration owner, pilot module, data permission, baseline, success threshold, pilot quote, signed scope, decision, source links and rights, demo URL, screenshot verification and next action.</p>'+a('buyer-account','Inspect the simulated buyer account','textlink')))
